<p>Freeze damage and burst pipe claims are not something most McAllen property owners think about. Our winters are usually mild, and many homes have plumbing in exterior walls, attics, or unprotected outdoor runs. Then a rare arctic outbreak arrives, temperatures stay below freezing for hours, and water lines split. When the thaw comes, so does the water.</p>

<p>This guide explains how freeze damage and burst pipe claims usually work in the Rio Grande Valley, what policy language to watch for, which costs are commonly disputed, and how to document the loss. It is general information. Your policy and the facts of your loss decide coverage.</p>

