<p>Notice the duration. On the first night, temperatures in southern Hidalgo County fell below freezing around 8:30 PM and did not climb back above 32°F until around 2:00 PM the next day. That is a long time for unprotected pipes in a region where plumbing is rarely designed with prolonged freezes in mind. Many pipes freeze without bursting until the thaw, which is why leaks often showed up a day or two after the coldest night.</p>

